abstract: >-
  We construct an operator calculus linking prime decomposition, occupation parity and
  additive response on spectral natural-number arithmetic. Prime residue classes form
  the augmentation cotangent basis, and the corresponding one-word vectors span the
  degree-one Hodge kernel. The complementary gap is exactly one, giving sharp heat and
  resolvent approximations to the prime projection with summable Gaussian trace errors.
  Symmetric and exterior occupations retain logarithmic arithmetic energy and evaluated
  quadratic correlation energy. A faithful extension of addition records relative
  inputs. Its charge defect relates input multiplicative parity to the parity of the
  sum, while Schur reduction retains the transverse contribution to the inverse
  response. Prime-direction transfer and mutually inverse square-dilation transforms
  connect the signed occupation responses. Combining additive and decomposition
  responses gives an endpoint map whose unique stable fixed point, under diagonal
  self-consistency, is enclosed with its infinite tail. Compact Laplace realizations of
  square energy and quadratic shell capacity have dimension three. In the stated
  spherical and central-sign classes, their coefficient functions admit a common
  Gaussian history calculus. Occupation traces and classical boundary arguments recover
  Bertrand's theorem, the prime-number asymptotic and square-free sign densities on the
  generated carrier.
